// NOTE (AI): Three flight families in one file. Vanilla mode is client-side physics only: it drives motionY and horizontal speed and sends no packets at all, with an anti-kick fall/ascend packet pair every 700ms so the server keeps receiving vertical oscillation. Damage mode floods C0CPacketInput + C03(true) every pre tick and triggers the fall-damage self-hit on enable with the canonical C04 ladder (y+3.05 false, y false, y+0.41999998688697815 true), which grants the damage boost that lets flight bypass NCP's flight checks. Verus mode uses a C08 block placement below the player plus motionY=0. The PacketOutEvent handler cancels C0FPacketConfirmTransaction and C00PacketKeepAlive entirely, which is what lets the position stream survive on servers that correlate transaction timing.

